From e0548e427d8c59db5d7abac2a8e4850fff5957e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:03:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/display: SSD1306 monochrome OLED driver, the OLED W Click

ssd1306 on SPI with D/C# and RES#: the three addressing modes, start
line, re-map, MUX, COM scan direction, offset and pin layout, inverse,
entire-on, display on/off and the charge pump (the panel lights only
with it), drawn through PpPanel. Its panel geometry is properties; the
defaults are the OLED W Click's MI9639BO-W (96x39, SEG95..0, COM19..0
and COM50..32 interleaved).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst |  12 +
 hw/display/meson.build                |   3 +-
 hw/display/ssd1306.c                  | 466 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 hw/misc/mikrobus.c                    |   7 +
 include/hw/display/ssd1306.h          |  19 ++
 5 files changed, 506 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 hw/display/ssd1306.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/display/ssd1306.h

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
index 24c0655..98af643 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
@@ -183,6 +183,18 @@ headers, so one UART Click at a time; it then takes SERCOM3's place in
   counter kept between transfers, reads wrapping at 256 KiB. Erased at
   power-up. ``view-at`` (hex) and ``view`` show 32 bytes for front ends.
 
+``oledw``
+  OLED W Click (v100): an SSD1306 (``ssd1306``) with a 96x39 white OLED
+  (MI9639BO-W) on SPI (jumpers J1-J3 on SPI), CS# on CS, D/C# on PWM, RES#
+  on RST (no pull resistors). Page, horizontal and vertical addressing,
+  start line, re-map, MUX, COM direction, offset and layout, inverse and
+  entire-on are modelled; the panel lights only with the display on and the
+  charge pump enabled (8Dh 14h). Panel: SEG95..0 left to right, COM19..0
+  and COM50..32 interleaved top to bottom (``seg-left``, ``com-row0``,
+  ``com-row1``); its picture is ``frame``/``frame-gen`` like the OLED C's.
+  Scrolling is not modelled. The OLED B Click (I2C only, v101) is not in
+  the catalog yet.
+
 SPI Clicks on both headers share the SPI bus; each listens only while its
 own CS is low (or, for the 74HC595 and MAX7219, latches on its own CS).
 
